# Line-ending policy. dk hashes every asset by its raw bytes, so each file
# must check out with the same endings on every platform. A Windows runner
# checks text out with CRLF (core.autocrlf=true), which gave the Windows legs
# different asset values from the Linux and macOS legs, and combine then
# published one key bound to two values. So every text file is LF; only the
# Windows launchers, which are not assets, keep their stored CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd -text
